                <pb facs="0645" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg521"/>

                <head>No. 317.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25, 1881</date>.
                        (Received April 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 147.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose the copy of a
                    letter which I received this morning from Mr. Boyton, and of my answer thereto.
                    * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>




